course: dictionary
lesson: 1625
title: Chesty and the chest
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When you have a cold, your chest can fill up with mucus, which is thick, sticky stuff. A cough that comes from this is wet and deep, and we call it chesty. «A chesty cough» means a deep, wet cough from a full chest.
explain: The clues in a text help you check. «A chesty cough, body aches or a tummy bug are «below the neck» signs, and hard exercise then makes you sicker and slower to recover.» Chesty is listed with body aches and a tummy bug, which are signs of being unwell, so it must mean the cough shows you are ill.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to test it. «A chesty cough» becomes «a wet cough from a full chest», and that still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning. Chesty is only used like this in everyday talk in places such as the UK, Ireland and Australia.
fact: «Chesty» is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a cough or a cold.
fact: «Chesty» means having a lot of mucus in the chest from a cold, with a deep, wet cough.
fact: Common phrases are «a chesty cough» and «a chesty cold».
fact: Cough medicine boxes in the UK, Ireland and Australia often say «for chesty coughs» and «for dry coughs», so the label tells you which kind of cough the medicine is for.
exercise: Ravi has a chesty cold and cannot play football today. What does chesty mean? | Having lots of mucus in the chest from a cold | Running fast and out of breath | Feeling very hot and sweaty | *Having a deep, wet cough from a full chest
exercise: «A runny nose with no fever may allow gentle play, but a chesty cough means no sport today.» Why does the author say no sport? | *A chesty cough is a sign you are unwell, so hard exercise could make you sicker | Sport is always cancelled on Tuesdays | A runny nose is a sign to run faster | A chesty cough means you have won a prize
exercise: The cough medicine box says «for dry coughs» and «for chesty coughs». Which cough is the chesty one? | sore | tickly | dry | *wet, from a full chest
test: Mum says, «You have a chesty cold, so rest today.» What does chesty tell you about your cold? | It makes you sneeze all day | *Your chest is full of mucus and you cough deeply | Your chest is very big | It has made your nose blocked
test: Which of these is a chesty cough? | A dry, tickly cough with no mucus | A cough that only happens at night | *A deep, wet cough from a full chest | A loud shout at a football match
exam: Jayden thinks chesty means fat or big. What does it really mean? | *Lots of mucus in the chest from a cold, with a deep, wet cough | Being very tall and thin | Lots of mucus in the chest from a cold, with a wet cough | Having a sore throat only
